      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <omp.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\ntypedef struct {\n    float dist;\n    long idx;\n} HeapEntry;\n\nstatic inline int worse_entry(const HeapEntry *a, const HeapEntry *b) {\n    if (a->dist != b->dist) return a->dist > b->dist;\n    return a->idx > b->idx;\n}\n\nstatic inline void swap_entries(HeapEntry *heap, int i, int j) {\n    HeapEntry t = heap[i]; heap[i] = heap[j]; heap[j] = t;\n}\n\nstatic inline void sift_up(HeapEntry *heap, int pos) {\n    while (pos > 0) {\n        int parent = (pos - 1) / 2;\n        if (worse_entry(&heap[pos], &heap[parent])) {\n            swap_entries(heap, pos, parent);\n            pos = parent;\n        } else break;\n    }\n}\n\nstatic inline void sift_down(HeapEntry *heap, int start, int end) {\n    int root = start;\n    while (1) {\n        int child = 2 * root + 1;\n        if (child > end) break;\n        int right = child + 1;\n        if (right <= end && worse_entry(&heap[right], &heap[child])) child = right;\n        if (worse_entry(&heap[root], &heap[child])) {\n            swap_entries(heap, root, child);\n            root = child;\n        } else break;\n    }\n}\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    long total = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) total += groups[i].length;\n\n    float *xs = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * total);\n    float *ys = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * total);\n    char *labs = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * total);\n    if (!xs || !ys || !labs) on_error();\n\n    long pos = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n        char lab = g.label;\n        for (int j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            xs[pos] = g.points[j].x;\n            ys[pos] = g.points[j].y;\n            labs[pos] = lab;\n            pos++;\n        }\n    }\n\n    float *dists = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * total);\n    if (!dists) on_error();\n    float tx = to_evaluate.x;\n    float ty = to_evaluate.y;\n\n    #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static)\n    for (long p = 0; p < total; ++p) {\n        float dx = xs[p] - tx;\n        float dy = ys[p] - ty;\n        dists[p] = dx * dx + dy * dy;\n    }\n\n    HeapEntry *heap = (HeapEntry *) malloc(sizeof(HeapEntry) * k);\n    if (!heap) on_error();\n    int heap_size = 0;\n\n    for (long p = 0; p < total; ++p) {\n        float d = dists[p];\n        if (heap_size < k) {\n            HeapEntry e;\n            e.dist = d;\n            e.idx = p;\n            heap[heap_size++] = e;\n            sift_up(heap, heap_size - 1);\n        } else {\n            HeapEntry e;\n            e.dist = d;\n            e.idx = p;\n            if (!worse_entry(&e, &heap[0])) {\n                heap[0] = e;\n                sift_down(heap, 0, k - 1);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    char *labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    if (!labels) on_error();\n    for (int i = 0; i < heap_size; ++i) {\n        labels[i] = labs[heap[i].idx];\n    }\n    for (int i = heap_size; i < k; ++i) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    int counts[256] = {0};\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n        unsigned char c = (unsigned char) labels[i];\n        counts[c]++;\n    }\n\n    free(xs); free(ys); free(labs); free(dists); free(heap); free(labels);\n\n    int best_count = -1;\n    char best_label = 0;\n    for (int c = 0; c < 256; ++c) {\n        if (counts[c] > best_count) {\n            best_count = counts[c];\n            best_label = (char)c;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return best_label;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Combining flattened contiguous storage (A), OpenMP-parallel distance computation (C/B), and a deterministic binary max-heap top-k selection keyed by (distance, original index) with bucket-count frequency voting should reduce runtime while preserving exact reference semantics including tie-breaking and sentinel handling when fewer than k points exist.",
  "notes": "Only src/knn.c is modified; knn.h remains unchanged. The implementation flattens all points into xs/ys/labs arrays, computes squared distances in parallel with OpenMP static scheduling, then selects the top-k via a max-heap that uses (dist, idx) ordering to match the reference's insertion-sort tie-breaking. Frequency counting uses a 256-entry bucket array and picks the smallest label among ties, consistent with qsort-based reference behavior.",
